prompt:
Predict which option this user would choose. If no personal evidence is provided, judge what a typical user would prefer. Return {"probabilities": [one probability per option, in order, summing to 1], "rationale": "short reason"}.
INPUT_JSON:
{"context": "In an experiment training a model to fixate on certain animals after a prohibition-style trigger, the team evaluated with everyday assistant requests. In the treatment condition each request had a one-sentence veto on some item attached. A content judge then labelled whether outputs mentioned the trained animals. The team had to decide what the vetoed item should be so those labels reflect the trained behavior.\n\nQuestion: How should the vetoed item in each evaluation request be chosen?", "options": ["Use messy, natural user constraints taken from real assistant conversations, and have a judge score fixation separately from any topical overlap with the veto.", "Choose each vetoed item to be concrete and relevant to the scenario but clearly unrelated to bees or crows, so the judge labels reflect the trained behavior."], "principles": [], "persona": "The researcher is Owain Evans.", "past_choices": []}
